[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790931261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2790931261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2790931261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mWjs9","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T20:30:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T20:30:33Z","body":"`get_class()` has been subject to a fair bit of counter-intuitive behavior regarding `class_name`, which also changed subtly over the versions: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/21789\r\n\r\nIf we already introduce a new method and suggest that users migrate away from `get_class()`, should we address some of these issues? This would be a unique opportunity to change behavior without breaking existing code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790931261/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790947361","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2790947361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2790947361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mWnoh","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T20:39:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T20:53:07Z","body":"> `get_class()` has been subject to a fair bit of counter-intuitive behavior regarding `class_name`, which also changed subtly over the versions: #21789\r\n> \r\n> If we already introduce a new method and suggest that users migrate away from `get_class()`, should we address some of these issues? This would be a unique opportunity to change behavior without breaking existing code.\r\n\r\nThat's an excellent suggestion! I think this makes a lot of sense.\r\nThat would also mean we'd have to change the behavior internally (currently, `get_class_name` returns the internal most derived class name, not any of the scripting ones).\r\n\r\n... which probably means renaming the existing `get_class_name` to something like `get_hard_class_name` ('hard' referring to non-script types, as described in my recent proposal https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12155). And assessing every caller which it should actually use.\r\n\r\nIf we decide for this, it will take a while to get there. But I'd be fully on board, and this PR isn't urgent or anything.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790947361/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791322326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2791322326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2791322326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mYDLW","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T01:30:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T01:30:31Z","body":"Common warning \"batches\" aren't a bad idea; maybe something like this in `typedefs.h`?\r\n```cpp\r\n#define GODOT_IGNORE_DEPRECATED_BEGIN /\r\n\tGODOT_GCC_WARNING_PUSH_AND_IGNORE(\"-Wdeprecated-declarations\") /\r\n\tGODOT_CLANG_WARNING_PUSH_AND_IGNORE(\"-Wdeprecated-declarations\") /\r\n\tGODOT_MSVC_WARNING_PUSH_AND_IGNORE(4996)\r\n#define GODOT_IGNORE_DEPRECATED_END /\r\n\tGODOT_MSVC_WARNING_POP /\r\n\tGODOT_CLANG_WARNING_POP /\r\n\tGODOT_GCC_WARNING_POP\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791322326/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791573029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2791573029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2791573029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mZAYl","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T05:07:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T05:07:31Z","body":"Note that there is [`is_class()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-is-class) that also uses `String` instead of `StringName`. However, `is_class_name()` sounds confusing (as if this method checks whether the passed argument is a class name, rather than checking whether the object is an instance of the class with the specified name), unlike `get_class_name()`. We should think about what naming would be consistent and clear. For example, `get_class_sn()` and `is_class_sn()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791573029/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791777184","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2791777184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2791777184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mZyOg","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T07:11:58Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T07:11:58Z","body":"Or `is_instance_of(class)`, which has prior art in many programming languages.\r\n\r\nImo clearer than `is_class` because that one sounds like \"is exactly the class\" (not inherited from it). \r\nThere are also other APIs using this terminology (`instance_from_id`, `Object.get_instance_id`, `ClassDB.instantiate`)...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791777184/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791803975","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2791803975","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2791803975,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mZ4xH","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T07:24:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T07:24:09Z","body":"I'm on the `is_instance_of` side; `is_class` has mislead me to think as you described before.\nWe don't necessarily need an `is_instance_of_name` alias because we can just do the python thing and \"interpret\" the argument as a class. so if we did have higher oder classes it could theoretically use the same function.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791803975/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794218937","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2794218937","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2794218937,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mjGW5","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T15:22:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T15:22:25Z","body":"> Or `is_instance_of(class)`, which has prior art in many programming languages.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, [`is_instance_of()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40gdscript.html#class-gdscript-method-is-instance-of) already exists as a global GDScript function. Adding a method with the same name, especially in the root class `Object`, would cause a conflict. If I remember correctly, global functions have higher priority during name lookup, so you would always have to use `self.is_instance_of()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794218937/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2839586716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2839586716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2839586716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pQKec","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-29T16:54:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-29T16:54:53Z","body":"The addition of a new `get_class_name()` that would return any script class_name set would be great for debugging and serialization of custom class objects. Regarding trying to add some corresponding new version of `is_class()` I think big issue with the current implementation is the discrepancy between that and the `is` operator ( as you might expect `my_object.is_class(\"MyClass\")` be the same as `my_object is MyClass`) see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12334). \r\n\r\nHowever, since we already have the `is` operator for most of these cases, maybe there isn't then such a pressing need for a new version of the `is_class()` function on Object as well if that would return the same result?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2839586716/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2941902377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2941902377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":2941902377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vWd4p","user":{"login":"RusheNewman","id":195997172,"node_id":"U_kgDOC66t9A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195997172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman","html_url":"https://github.com/RusheNewman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RusheNewman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T23:19:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T23:22:49Z","body":"+1 to the @lostminds comment, this would be very useful for serialization.\r\n\r\nI am also currently working on something that would greatly benefit from this- a trait or component system where an object's logic is dictated by the components that it consists of. In order to quickly iterate through them, all the components are stored in a  `Dictionary[StringName, ItemTrait]`, where the keys are the `StringName`s of the traits. Right now, I need to override a custom function that returns the trait name inside of each and every `ItemTrait` I define:\r\n```gdscript\r\nstatic func get_class_name() -> StringName: return &\"ItemTrait\"\r\n```\r\nBut, of course, this is a lot of boilerplate and I would really love to avoid that.\r\n\r\nAlso, would this function be static? That would be extremely useful because then something like this would be possible:\r\n```gdscript\r\nitem.get_trait(ItemTrait.get_class_name())\r\n```\r\nIf anything, get_class() should have already been a static function.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2941902377/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595722074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-4595722074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":4595722074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEe0nWg","user":{"login":"jauwnio","id":157239827,"node_id":"U_kgDOCV9KEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157239827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio","html_url":"https://github.com/jauwnio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T19:17:36Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T19:17:36Z","body":"this is something I feel really strongly about and wanted to help work on, is there anything that I can add to help get this PR in a state that it can be submitted for review?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595722074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595769144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-4595769144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":4595769144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEe3fOA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T19:24:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T19:24:37Z","body":"@jauwnio What part of the PR do you feel strongly about, and why?\r\nI intend to rebase it some time but we've postponed progression because we're not quite sure what final shape the method should get (e.g. whether GDScript class names should be returned too).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595769144/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595947151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-4595947151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":4595947151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEfCWjw","user":{"login":"jauwnio","id":157239827,"node_id":"U_kgDOCV9KEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157239827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio","html_url":"https://github.com/jauwnio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T19:49:54Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T20:00:09Z","body":">@jauwnio What part of the PR do you feel strongly about, and why? I intend to rebase it some time but we've postponed progression because we're not quite sure what final shape the method should get (e.g. whether GDScript class names should be returned too).\r\n\r\nFor my specific use case, I have a lot of \"buildings\" which all extend custom class \"Building\". These different types of buildings are all their own class_name, such as `OilFactory` or `OilStorage`, which extends `Building`.\r\n\r\nWhen the player is interacting with buildings, I want to be able to easily check what type of building we're working with. Since they all have their own unique class, just checking the class would suffice as it would be the most \"truthful\" way of figuring out what building I'm working with.\r\n\r\nI have, let's say 20 different total buildings. Certain buildings can interact with only certain other buildings, so I was using a big match statement to handle those unique cases.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar building_class := building1.get_class()\r\nmatch building_class:\r\n    OilGenerator:\r\n        foo\r\n    OilStorage:\r\n        bar\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut that doesn't work, since `get_class()` returns the base class, not my custom class.\r\n\r\nThis is the workaround that I implemented, which was mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/21789 where the `is` keyword behaves differently than `get_class()`:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc set_connection(building1 : Building, building2 : Building) -> void:\r\n    if building1 is OilGenerator:\r\n          foo\r\n    if building1 is OilStorage:\r\n          bar\r\n           \r\n```\r\n\r\nI think functionally it's not any different but it is a lot less pretty. It does work perfectly, though, which makes this not an urgent issue, so I understand why it has been postponed.\r\n\r\nAs to where that links up to this PR...\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, a `get_class_name()` should just return whatever you have specified in `class_name`. That is what would make the most sense. Additionally. `get_class()` as it is today should also still exist, and that should return the base class name, as it does today. Kind of like how you mentioned `get_hard_class_name()`.\r\n\r\nI've had this issue in my mind since the last game jam entry I did but didn't think of it again until today I randomly came across this video and timestamp here: https://youtu.be/U-8ZRATnkmo?si=V9XDwnJ9wFgCqiqd&t=418 where another dev shares basically the exact same confusion as myself. Plus there's a number of reddit threads asking the same question as well so I think this would be a good thing to help make working with custom classes more pleasant","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4595947151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4596056883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-4596056883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":4596056883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEfJDMw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T20:05:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T20:05:18Z","body":"Right, thank you for explaining.\r\n\r\nThe PR in its current form does not what you would hope it does. It merely returns the `get_class` name as a `StringName` instead of a `String`. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/21789 is _not_ addressed in the current implementation.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4596056883/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4596156107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-4596156107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105215","id":4596156107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEfPGyw","user":{"login":"jauwnio","id":157239827,"node_id":"U_kgDOCV9KEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157239827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio","html_url":"https://github.com/jauwnio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-01T20:17:59Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T20:17:59Z","body":"> Right, thank you for explaining.\r\n> \r\n> The PR in its current form does not what you would hope it does. It merely returns the `get_class` name as a `StringName` instead of a `String`. #21789 is _not_ addressed in the current implementation.\r\n\r\nAh, I see. I was led here by Calinou's comment on this proposal https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12334 which said that this would fix the script class name confusion\r\n\r\nI would think though that this PR should come first before adding a new method to pull the script class name, though, would that be correct? Because any implementation of `get_custom_class_name` or whatever would ideally be `StringName`\r\n\r\nBasically what I am saying is that I want to make a PR to address that proposal then if you don't think that this one properly addresses my use case (which seems to be the same as @lostminds' concerns). But if I want to do that, should I wait until this is decided on, since ultimately it's not a true blocking issue since there are many different workarounds","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4596156107/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]